## Propagation review

### cancelPrompt during context creation

```text
cancelPrompt()
-> parent rejects/closes request quickly
-> request cancel MessagePort reaches worker
-> abortActiveRequest()
-> record.contextController.abort(...)
-> createContext boundary settles
-> worker does not enter session.prompt(...)
```

### resetSession during context creation

```text
resetSession(sessionId)
-> parent cancels matching requests
-> worker reset_session aborts matching active records
-> context createSignal is aborted
-> waitForActiveRequestBoundaries()
-> disposeSessionById()
-> reset_done only after boundary/disposal
```

### resetModel during context creation

```text
resetModel()
-> parent cancels all accepted requests
-> worker reset_model aborts all active records
-> context boundary settles
-> disposeModelStack()
-> model_reset_done only after safe disposal
```

### shutdown abort during context creation

```text
shutdownRuntime({ mode: "abort" })
-> parent cancels accepted work
-> worker shutdown aborts active context/prompt records
-> context boundary settles
-> model.dispose happens after boundary
-> shutdown_done
```

### drain modes

```text
plain drain:
accepted context creation is not aborted.

drain-with-timeout:
context creation abort happens only after timeout-driven cancellation.
```

### context retry

```text
genuine context creation failure still retries.
cancel/reset/shutdown during context creation does not retry.
ignored createSignal fallback waits for createContext to return, disposes partial artifacts, and avoids prompt start.
```

